From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dariusz Majnert <dariusz.majnert@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:09:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] task: drop interrupted MDI call state whenever the
 interpreter is reset

An MDI command that runs a remap (or an O-word call) and has to wait for
its queue to drain leaves task with continuation state: mdi_execute_level,
mdi_execute_wait and mdi_execute_next, which make task call
interp.execute(NULL) to resume the call once the queue is empty.
mdi_execute_abort() clears that state, but only some abort paths call it.

emcTaskAbort() closes and resets the interpreter, which unwinds the call
stack, yet the callers in emctask.cc cannot reach the static
mdi_execute_abort(): emcTaskSetState() for E-stop, machine off and E-stop
reset, emcTaskSetMode() for MDI and AUTO, the ON to not-ON edge in
emcTaskUpdate() and the error path of emcTaskPlanSynch(). In all of these
the stale state survives, and when the machine is back on in MDI mode task
resumes a call that no longer exists. For a Python remap that segfaults
milltask in Interp::execute_call() (no executing remap); for an NGC remap
the MDI command never finishes. Commands queued behind the interrupted one
also survived and ran after the machine was re-enabled.

Make mdi_execute_abort() visible to emctask.cc and call it at the end of
emcTaskAbort(), right after the interpreter reset. The existing explicit
calls next to emcTaskAbort() are left as they are; a second call is a
no-op.

tests/remap/mdi-remap-abort interrupts a waiting NGC and a waiting Python
remap with each of E-stop, machine off, a mode change and an abort followed
by an interpreter re-init once idle, and checks that milltask survives and
MDI works afterwards.
---
 src/emc/task/emctask.cc     | 4 ++++
 src/emc/task/emctaskmain.cc | 2 +-
 src/emc/task/task.hh        | 1 +
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/emc/task/emctask.cc b/src/emc/task/emctask.cc
index f889dd3..b6793d2 100644
--- a/src/emc/task/emctask.cc
+++ b/src/emc/task/emctask.cc
@@ -282,6 +282,10 @@ int emcTaskAbort()
 	}
     }
 
+    // the reset above unwound any call an interrupted MDI command was
+    // inside of, so its continuation and queued MDI commands go too
+    mdi_execute_abort();
+
     return 0;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/emc/task/emctaskmain.cc b/src/emc/task/emctaskmain.cc
index 57b8240..3e8c047 100644
--- a/src/emc/task/emctaskmain.cc
+++ b/src/emc/task/emctaskmain.cc
@@ -817,7 +817,7 @@ interpret_again:
 		}		// if interp len is less than max
 }
 
-static void mdi_execute_abort(void)
+void mdi_execute_abort(void)
 {
     int queued_mdi_commands;
 
diff --git a/src/emc/task/task.hh b/src/emc/task/task.hh
index 4a7089e..4220b67 100644
--- a/src/emc/task/task.hh
+++ b/src/emc/task/task.hh
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ int emcTaskInit();
 int emcTaskHalt();
 int emcTaskStateRestore();
 int emcTaskAbort();
+void mdi_execute_abort(void);
 void emcTaskCancelAvailability();
 int emcTaskSetMode(EMC_TASK_MODE mode);
 int emcTaskSetState(EMC_TASK_STATE state);
